course: dictionary
lesson: 7575
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. The word press is a good example. Its meaning depends on the words around it, which are its context. «Press the green flag again to start the scripts.» Here press means push with your finger.
explain: «For a small cut, press with a clean cloth to stop bleeding.» Press here means push firmly on something. Try the swap test: put push in place of press, and if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning. Pushing on a cut to stop it bleeding makes sense.
explain: Press can also mean to iron clothes flat, or to try hard to make someone do something. In a science text, press might mean squeeze flat, as in pressing flowers to dry them. Look at the clues around the word, then decide which meaning fits.
explain: Press can be a noun too. A press is a machine that pushes, squeezes or prints. The press means newspapers, TV news and the people who write them. Phrases like «press on» (keep going) and «pressed for time» (in a hurry) need the whole phrase to make sense.
fact: Press is a verb and a noun. As a verb it has several meanings, and the context tells you which one is meant.
fact: «Press» can mean to push firmly on something, as in «press the button».
fact: «Press» can also mean to iron clothes flat.
fact: «Press» can mean to try hard to make someone do something.
fact: The press means newspapers, TV news and the people who write them.
exercise: «Press the green flag again to start the scripts.» What does press mean here? | Squeeze out juice | *Push with your finger | Newspapers | Iron flat
exercise: Mum says, «Could you press my blue shirt before school?» What does press mean? | To wash it in cold water | To pull it off quickly | To hide it in a drawer | *To iron it flat
exercise: «The scientist pressed the flowers between two books to dry them.» What does pressed mean here? | Painted bright | Picked from the garden | *Squeezed flat | Put in a vase
test: «For a small cut, press with a clean cloth to stop bleeding.» What is the best meaning of press here? | Iron flat | *Push firmly on | Print | Newspapers
test: Ella says, «Our teacher is pressed for time today.» What does pressed for time mean? | Very bored | Stuck in traffic | *In a hurry | Happy with the clock
exam: Which sentence uses press to mean newspapers and TV news? | Press the red button to stop the machine | *The press reported the story about the new school | Mum will press my shirt tonight | Pressed for time, Sam ran to the bus
